# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenRecapper configuration. Copy to `.env` and fill in your own values.
# Each operator/fork must bring their OWN Discord app, Deepgram account, and
# (optionally) storage bucket + relay. No shared credentials are provided.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From the Discord Developer Portal (see DISCORD_SETUP.md).
DISCORD_TOKEN=your-bot-token
# Multiple tokens = concurrent recordings per server (primary first); DISCORD_TOKEN still works for single-bot setups
# DISCORD_TOKENS=primary-token,recorder2-token
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=your-application-id
# Deepgram API key for speech-to-text (https://console.deepgram.com/).
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=your-deepgram-api-key

# ── General (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Display name used in startup-alert DMs and email subjects.
BOT_NAME=OpenRecapper
# Comma-separated names shown in /record's required name picker.
RECORD_MEETING_NAMES=UNNAMED-MEETING
# Where to write recordings on disk (defaults to ./recordings).
# RECORDINGS_DIR=/var/lib/openrecapper/recordings
# Discord user ID to DM if a startup health check fails (e.g. dead Deepgram key).
# ALERT_DISCORD_USER_ID=
CHARACTER_DM_USER_IDS=363119992214126593
CHARACTER_DEFINITIONS=Kasane:E74C3C,Shiki:F1C40F,Conrad:000000,Guava:E67E22,Arsene:3498DB,Mello:795548,NPC:2ECC71

# ── AI summaries & email (optional, via a relay service) ─────────────────────
# Summaries + email are produced by a small companion "relay" HTTP service that
# you run and point at your own LLM provider + email gateway. If RELAY_TOKEN is
# left blank the bot still records + transcribes; summaries/email are skipped.
# See README “AI summaries & email” for the expected relay API.
# RELAY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787
# RELAY_TOKEN=your-shared-relay-secret
# The two gateway URLs below are read by the RELAY (e.g. relay-exedev/server.mjs),
# not by the bot. They're listed here for one-place configuration when you run
# the relay with this env file; under systemd, set them in the unit's
# Environment= lines instead. exe.dev users: look up the current gateway
# addresses in the exe.dev docs (https://exe.dev/docs.md).
# RELAY_LLM_GATEWAY=your-llm-gateway-url
# RELAY_EMAIL_GATEWAY=your-email-gateway-url
# Model name passed through to your relay/LLM provider (blank = relay default).
# SUMMARY_MODEL=
# Tunes the summary template wording (e.g. "engineering standup", "book club").
# SUMMARY_GROUP_NAME=study group
# Email the summary + transcript links here after each call.
# SUMMARY_EMAIL_TO=you@example.com

# ── GitHub issue filing via /openrecapper-issue (optional) ───────────────────
# Users describe a bug/feature in plain text; the relay LLM drafts a title +
# description and the bot files it directly on GitHub. Needs all three below.
# Use a fine-grained PAT scoped to "Issues: Read & Write" on just the one repo.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...
# GITHUB_OWNER=your-org-or-user
# GITHUB_REPO=your-repo
# Comma-separated recipients emailed when an issue is filed (needs the relay).
# Standalone — if unset, no issue emails are sent (no fallback to SUMMARY_EMAIL_TO).
# ISSUE_EMAIL_TO=you@example.com
# Discord user IDs (comma-separated) to cc/@-mention at the end of the public
# reply when an issue is filed. Empty = no cc line.
# ISSUE_CC_USER_IDS=111111111111111111,222222222222222222

# ── Cloud archival to S3-compatible storage (optional, e.g. Cloudflare R2) ────
# If these are unset, recordings/transcripts stay on local disk only. Upload is
# enabled when ACCESS_KEY_ID + SECRET_ACCESS_KEY + ENDPOINT are all present.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_BUCKET=your-bucket-name
# R2_ENDPOINT=https://<accountid>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# R2_PUBLIC_URL=https://your-public-bucket-url

# ── Scheduled recording ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Standing-call schedules are now managed at runtime via the `/schedule` slash
# command (ManageGuild) and persisted to data/schedules.json. You normally do
# NOT need any env vars here.
#
# Optional: override where schedules are stored.
# SCHEDULES_FILE=/var/lib/openrecapper/schedules.json
#
# ── Legacy one-time seed (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# These SCHEDULED_* vars are ONLY read once, to seed the first schedule the very
# first time the bot starts WITHOUT a data/schedules.json file. After that file
# exists they are ignored entirely — the JSON store is the source of truth.
# SCHEDULED_GUILD_ID=
# SCHEDULED_VOICE_CHANNEL_ID=
# SCHEDULED_TEXT_CHANNEL_ID=
# SCHEDULED_CRON=15 11 * * 1,5
# SCHEDULED_TIMEZONE=America/New_York
# SCHEDULED_NAME=Standing call
